<title>USA: Snyder Oil to redeem convertible notes.</title>
<headline>Snyder Oil to redeem convertible notes.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WORTH, Texas 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Snyder Oil Corp said Wednesday it had called for redemption on July 1 its convertible subordinated notes due May 15, 2001.</p>
<p>The notes will be redeemed at 103.51 percent of principal, plus accrued interest.</p>
<p>The company has about $81.6 million of the notes outstanding.</p>
<p>The notes were issued in May 1994 and are convertible into common stock at $22.57 per share.</p>
<p>Snyder shares were off 5/8 at 17-5/8.</p>
<p>Holders of the notes may convert them into common stock on or before June 24.</p>
